# MDM Application — Full Improvement Sprint Task List

## Phase 1: Critical Bug Fixes (Blocking Production)

### 1.1 — Unify WebSocket Command Message Shape (Backend + Android)
- [ ] Update `CommandService.notifyDeviceOfCommand` to emit `commandType`+`commandId`+`payload` fields (not `command`+`parameters`)
- [ ] Update [WebSocketClient.kt](file:///c:/code/MDM/android-app/app/src/main/java/com/mdm/app/websocket/WebSocketClient.kt) [handleCommand](file:///c:/code/MDM/android-app/app/src/main/java/com/mdm/app/websocket/WebSocketClient.kt#241-261) to parse `commandType`/`commandId`/`payload` and delegate to `MainActivity.handleServerCommand`
- [ ] Add a `commandListener` interface/callback so [WebSocketClient](file:///c:/code/MDM/android-app/app/src/main/java/com/mdm/app/websocket/WebSocketClient.kt#14-474) can call into [MainActivity](file:///c:/code/MDM/android-app/app/src/main/java/com/mdm/app/MainActivity.kt#30-758)
- [ ] Unify [handleDeviceLock](file:///c:/code/MDM/android-app/app/src/main/java/com/mdm/app/websocket/WebSocketClient.kt#324-340), [handleDeviceWipe](file:///c:/code/MDM/android-app/app/src/main/java/com/mdm/app/websocket/WebSocketClient.kt#341-357) in [WebSocketClient](file:///c:/code/MDM/android-app/app/src/main/java/com/mdm/app/websocket/WebSocketClient.kt#14-474) to use the same dispatcher

### 1.2 — Authenticate WebSocket `deviceIdentify` Event (Backend)
- [ ] Issue a `deviceToken` JWT (role=DEVICE) during enrollment and return it to the device
- [ ] Update Android `WebSocketClient.onOpen` to send `deviceIdentify` with `{ deviceId, token }`
- [ ] Add token verification inside the `deviceIdentify` socket handler in [server.ts](file:///c:/code/MDM/backend/src/server.ts)

### 1.3 — Fix `deviceStatusUpdate` Socket Event Bug (Backend)
- [ ] Fetch device from DB first to get DB [id](file:///c:/code/MDM/backend/src/middleware/auth.ts#243-259) and `oldStatus` before running the update
- [ ] Fix `DeviceEvent.create` to use `device.id` (cuid), not `data.deviceId` (string)
- [ ] Fix logging so `oldStatus` and `newStatus` are actually different values

### 1.4 — Restrict Socket.IO CORS + Room Separation (Backend)
- [ ] Set Socket.IO CORS origin to use same allow-list as Express CORS (env-aware)
- [ ] Add `admin` room joining for dashboard clients on WebSocket [connection](file:///c:/code/MDM/android-app/app/src/main/java/com/mdm/app/websocket/WebSocketClient.kt#450-468)
- [ ] Replace all `io.emit(...)` with `io.to('admins').emit(...)` for dashboard events
- [ ] Keep `io.to('device_${deviceId}').emit(...)` for device-specific commands

### 1.5 — Rate-Limit Enrollment Endpoint (Backend)
- [ ] Add express-rate-limit middleware (5 req/min per IP) to `POST /api/devices/enroll`

### 1.6 — Add Missing Database Indexes (Backend)
- [ ] Add `@@index([lastSeen])` to [Device](file:///c:/code/MDM/android-app/app/src/main/java/com/mdm/app/websocket/WebSocketClient.kt#437-449) model in [schema.prisma](file:///c:/code/MDM/backend/prisma/schema.prisma)
- [ ] Add `@@index([status])` to `RemoteCommand` model
- [ ] Add `@@index([createdAt])` to `DeviceEvent` model
- [ ] Run `npx prisma migrate dev --name add_missing_indexes`

### 1.7 — Fix `cacheTime` → `gcTime` (Admin Dashboard)
- [ ] Rename `cacheTime` to `gcTime` in [App.tsx](file:///c:/code/MDM/admin-dashboard/src/App.tsx) React Query client config

