## Phase 2: High-Priority Feature Completions

### 2.1 — Admin Notification System (Admin Dashboard)
- [ ] Create `NotificationContext.tsx` listening to Socket.IO events: `commandFailed`, `deviceOffline`, `securityViolation`
- [ ] Add notification bell icon to `DashboardLayout` top bar
- [ ] Implement notification drawer showing last 20 alerts with timestamps
- [ ] Add backend emission for `deviceOffline` event in heartbeat monitor

### 2.2 — Kiosk Mode End-to-End (Admin Dashboard → Backend → Android)
- [ ] Add kiosk mode toggle card to device detail view (`DevicesPage`)
- [ ] Verify `POST /api/commands` accepts `ENABLE_KIOSK`/`DISABLE_KIOSK` command types
- [ ] Test full flow: admin toggles kiosk → backend queues command → device receives and executes

### 2.3 — Private Key Encryption at Rest (Backend)
- [ ] Create `CryptoService` with AES-256-GCM encrypt/decrypt using `ENCRYPTION_KEY` env var
- [ ] Wrap [certificateController.ts](file:///c:/code/MDM/backend/src/controllers/certificateController.ts) to encrypt `privateKey` before DB insert, decrypt on read

### 2.4 — Pagination for Device and Command Lists (Backend + Admin Dashboard)
- [ ] Add `page`/`limit` query params to `GET /api/devices` and `GET /api/commands`
- [ ] Update admin dashboard device list to use server-side pagination with MUI `TablePagination`

### 2.5 — Verify Policy Enforcement on Android
- [ ] Review [PolicyEngine.kt](file:///c:/code/MDM/android-app/app/src/main/java/com/mdm/app/policy/PolicyEngine.kt) for WiFi restriction, app blacklist, and password enforcement
- [ ] Verify [BootReceiver.kt](file:///c:/code/MDM/android-app/app/src/main/java/com/mdm/app/receivers/BootReceiver.kt) triggers policy re-application after device restart
- [ ] Test policy sync flow end-to-end

### 2.6 — Email Notifications for Critical Events (Backend)
- [ ] Add Nodemailer (or SendGrid) to backend dependencies
- [ ] Create `NotificationService.ts` with methods: `sendDeviceOfflineAlert`, `sendSecurityViolationAlert`, `sendCertExpiryAlert`
- [ ] Trigger from heartbeat monitor and security events

